	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:03,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3720
			},
			"text": " This question comes from Suzanne, who asks \"If you had a printed version of the whole"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,720",
				"to": "00:00:06,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3720,
				"to": 6880
			},
			"text": " of Wikipedia, how many printers would you need in order to keep up with the changes"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:06,880",
				"to": "00:00:08,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 6880,
				"to": 8680
			},
			"text": " made to the live version?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:08,680",
				"to": "00:00:13,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 8680,
				"to": 13560
			},
			"text": " For the English Wikipedia, you'd need this many."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:13,560",
				"to": "00:00:17,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 13560,
				"to": 17480
			},
			"text": " Six printers is surprisingly few, but before you try to create a live updating paper version"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:17,480",
				"to": "00:00:21,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 17480,
				"to": 21640
			},
			"text": " of Wikipedia, let's look at what those printers would be doing and how much they'd cost."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:21,640",
				"to": "00:00:23,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 21640,
				"to": 23760
			},
			"text": " People have considered printing out Wikipedia before."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:23,760",
				"to": "00:00:28,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 23760,
				"to": 28120
			},
			"text": " In 2012, Rob Matthews printed every featured article creating a book a couple feet thick,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:28,120",
				"to": "00:00:32,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 28120,
				"to": 32000
			},
			"text": " and in 2015, Michael Mandenberg created an art installation to show the scope of Wikipedia"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:32,000",
				"to": "00:00:35,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 32000,
				"to": 35600
			},
			"text": " by printing around 1% of its articles, although without images."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,600",
				"to": "00:00:37,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35600,
				"to": 37960
			},
			"text": " The entire encyclopedia would be a lot bigger."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:37,960",
				"to": "00:00:41,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 37960,
				"to": 41520
			},
			"text": " Wikipedia user TomPw has set up a Wikipedia page that calculates the current size of the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:41,520",
				"to": "00:00:44,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 41520,
				"to": 44600
			},
			"text": " whole English Wikipedia without images in printed volumes."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:44,600",
				"to": "00:00:48,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 44600,
				"to": 48320
			},
			"text": " It would currently fill a lot of bookshelves, but most libraries have far more books."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:48,320",
				"to": "00:00:50,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 48320,
				"to": 50120
			},
			"text": " Keeping up with the edits would be harder."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:50,120",
				"to": "00:00:54,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 50120,
				"to": 54560
			},
			"text": " English Wikipedia currently receives about 150,000 edits each day, or 100 per minute."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:54,560",
				"to": "00:00:58,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 54560,
				"to": 58320
			},
			"text": " We could try to define a way to measure the word count of the average edit, but that's"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:58,320",
				"to": "00:00:59,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 58320,
				"to": 59760
			},
			"text": " hard bordering on impossible."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:59,760",
				"to": "00:01:01,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 59760,
				"to": 61360
			},
			"text": " Unfortunately, we don't need to."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:01,360",
				"to": "00:01:04,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 61360,
				"to": 64880
			},
			"text": " We can just estimate that each change is going to require us to reprint a page somewhere."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:04,880",
				"to": "00:01:09,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 64880,
				"to": 69360
			},
			"text": " Now, many edits will actually change multiple pages, but many other edits are reverts, which"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:09,360",
				"to": "00:01:11,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 69360,
				"to": 71760
			},
			"text": " would let us put back pages that we've already printed."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:11,760",
				"to": "00:01:14,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 71760,
				"to": 74680
			},
			"text": " So one page per edit seems like a reasonable middle ground."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:14,680",
				"to": "00:01:18,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 74680,
				"to": 78720
			},
			"text": " For a mix of photos, tables, and text typical of Wikipedia, a Goodingjet printer might put"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:18,720",
				"to": "00:01:20,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 78720,
				"to": 80320
			},
			"text": " out 15 pages per minute."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:20,320",
				"to": "00:01:23,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 80320,
				"to": 83480
			},
			"text": " This means you'd only need about six printers running at any given time to keep pace with"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:23,480",
				"to": "00:01:25,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 83480,
				"to": 85240
			},
			"text": " the roughly 100 edits each minute."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:25,240",
				"to": "00:01:27,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 85240,
				"to": 87160
			},
			"text": " The paper would stack up quickly."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:27,160",
				"to": "00:01:30,280"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 87160,
				"to": 90280
			},
			"text": " Using Rob Matthews' book as a starting point, I did my own back of the envelope estimate"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:30,280",
				"to": "00:01:33,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 90280,
				"to": 93520
			},
			"text": " for the size of the current English Wikipedia, and based on the average length of featured"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:33,520",
				"to": "00:01:37,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 93520,
				"to": 97720
			},
			"text": " articles versus all articles, I came up with an estimate of 300 cubic meters for a printout"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:37,720",
				"to": "00:01:38,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 97720,
				"to": 98720
			},
			"text": " of the whole thing."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:38,720",
				"to": "00:01:41,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 98720,
				"to": 101760
			},
			"text": " By comparison, if you were trying to keep up with the edits, you'd be printing out 300"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:41,760",
				"to": "00:01:43,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 101760,
				"to": 103680
			},
			"text": " cubic meters every month."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:43,680",
				"to": "00:01:48,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 103680,
				"to": 108040
			},
			"text": " Six printers isn't that many, but they'd be running all the time, and that gets expensive."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:48,040",
				"to": "00:01:50,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 108040,
				"to": 110920
			},
			"text": " The electricity to run them would be cheap, a few dollars a day."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:50,920",
				"to": "00:01:54,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 110920,
				"to": 114120
			},
			"text": " The paper would be about one cent per sheet, which means you'd be spending about a thousand"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:54,120",
				"to": "00:01:55,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 114120,
				"to": 115120
			},
			"text": " dollars a day."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:55,120",
				"to": "00:01:59,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 115120,
				"to": 119200
			},
			"text": " You'd want to hire people to manage the printers 24/7, so depending on wages in your area this"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:59,200",
				"to": "00:02:02,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 119200,
				"to": 122900
			},
			"text": " could cost less than the paper, or much less if you can figure out a way to trick Wikipedia's"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:02,900",
				"to": "00:02:04,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 122900,
				"to": 124960
			},
			"text": " volunteer editors into helping you."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:04,960",
				"to": "00:02:08,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 124960,
				"to": 128360
			},
			"text": " Even the printers themselves wouldn't be too expensive, despite the terrifyingly fast"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:08,360",
				"to": "00:02:12,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 128360,
				"to": 132320
			},
			"text": " replacement cycle, but the ink cartridges would be a nightmare."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:12,320",
				"to": "00:02:15,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 132320,
				"to": 135400
			},
			"text": " Various sources estimate that for a typical inkjet printer, the real-life cost of ink"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:15,400",
				"to": "00:02:19,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 135400,
				"to": 139240
			},
			"text": " runs from five cents a page for black and white to around ten cents a page for color."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:19,240",
				"to": "00:02:23,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 139240,
				"to": 143240
			},
			"text": " With 150,000 daily page edits, that means you'd be spending about ten thousand dollars"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:23,240",
				"to": "00:02:27,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 143240,
				"to": 147680
			},
			"text": " per day on ink cartridges, so you'd definitely want to invest in a laser printer."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:27,680",
				"to": "00:02:32,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 147680,
				"to": 152000
			},
			"text": " Otherwise, in just a month or two, this project could end up costing you half a million dollars."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:32,000",
				"to": "00:02:33,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 152000,
				"to": 153720
			},
			"text": " But that's not even the worst part."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:33,720",
				"to": "00:02:38,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 153720,
				"to": 158160
			},
			"text": " If someday Wikipedia decides to go dark again, like they did in 2012, and you want to join"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:38,160",
				"to": "00:02:42,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 158160,
				"to": 162360
			},
			"text": " the protest, you're going to have to get giant creative markers so you can color every page"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:42,360",
				"to": "00:02:43,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 162360,
				"to": 163360
			},
			"text": " solid black."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:43,360",
				"to": "00:02:45,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 163360,
				"to": 165160
			},
			"text": " I would definitely stick to digital."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:49,240",
				"to": "00:02:56,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 169240,
